---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="FileLocker Terms of Service" 
  description="Read the FileLocker Terms of Service to understand the terms and conditions for using our browser-based file protection tools."
>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <div class="guide-hero">
    <div class="hero-shape hero-shape-1"></div>
    <div class="hero-shape hero-shape-2"></div>
    <div class="hero-inner" style="text-align:center; max-width:40rem;">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle" style="margin:0 auto;">
        Please read these terms carefully before using FileLocker.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="w-full bg-[#f8fafc] py-12 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <div class="content-card animate-fade-in-up">
        <div class="prose max-w-none">
          <h2>Acceptance of Terms</h2>
          <p>By accessing and using FileLocker ("the Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree to these terms, do not use the Service.</p>

          <h2>Description of Service</h2>
          <p>FileLocker is a browser-based file protection tool that processes files locally on your device. FileLocker does not upload your files to a server for processing.</p>

          <h2>User Responsibilities</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>You are solely responsible for keeping your passwords secure and recoverable.</li>
            <li>FileLocker cannot recover lost passwords under any circumstances.</li>
            <li>You must have the legal right to protect any files you process with FileLocker.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>FileLocker is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. We are not liable for any data loss, corruption, or damages arising from the use of the Service. Always maintain backups of your important files.</p>

          <h2>Privacy</h2>
          <p>Please refer to our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for information about how we handle your data.</p>

          <h2>Changes to Terms</h2>
          <p>We reserve the right to update these terms at any time. Continued use of the Service constitutes acceptance of any changes.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
